course: dictionary
lesson: 4402
title: Halal: what is allowed
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Halal means allowed. In Islam, it describes things that are permitted by Islamic law, and you will hear it most often about food. «Halal means allowed; halal food has no pork and Muslims do not drink alcohol.»
explain: The opposite of halal is haram, which means forbidden. So when someone asks «is it halal?», they want to know whether it is allowed.
explain: You will see the word in shops and canteens too. A «halal butcher» sells halal meat, and many school canteens and supermarkets in the UK, USA, Canada and Australia offer halal options.
explain: Learning what halal means helps you understand your Muslim friends. «You may have Muslim friends who fast, pray and keep halal food, and the right thing is to learn what they really believe and never to judge them by the worst things a few people do.»
fact: Halal means allowed by Islamic law.
fact: Halal is used especially for food: meat from animals killed in the correct way, and no pork or alcohol.
fact: A halal shop or restaurant sells halal food.
fact: The opposite of halal is haram, which means forbidden.
fact: Many pupils learn about halal food in religious education, and many school canteens offer halal options.
exercise: What does halal mean? | Forbidden in Islam | A kind of pudding | A place to pray | *Allowed by Islamic law
exercise: Which word is the opposite of halal? | Canteen | *Haram | Allowed | Halal butcher
exercise: Which shop would sell halal meat? | A bike shop | *A halal butcher | A shoe shop | A bakery that sells only cakes
test: Mia asks, «Is it halal?» What is she asking? | Whether the food is sweet | *Whether the food is allowed in Islam | Whether the shop is open | Whether the food is cold
test: Why might a Christian child learn what halal means? | To laugh at Muslim friends | To stop being friends with Muslims | *To understand Muslim friends and not judge them unfairly | To learn to cook pork
exam: Which sentence is true? | *Halal food has no pork, and Muslims do not drink alcohol | Halal means forbidden | Halal food has pork in it | Haram means allowed
